==County coding==
The current county-coding system on standard-issue Idaho license plates has been in use since 1945. The naming convention is the order of the county in an alphabetical list followed by the first letter of the county name. For example, <code>2T</code> indicates the second county beginning with <code>T</code> in an alphabetical list, or [[Twin Falls County, Idaho|Twin Falls County]]. If only one county begins with a particular letter, the letter alone serves as the county code. Specialty and [[Vehicle registration plates of the United States#Vanity and specialty plates|vanity]] license plates do not use county codes; some non-passenger types are county-coded, while others are not.
